Pipelined Fixed-Point Price Comparator
--------------------------------------

A low-latency, 2-stage pipelined fixed-point price threshold comparator written in Verilog.
Designed with high-frequency trading (HFT) principles in mind, this project demonstrates
deterministic timing, clean signal registration, and zero floating-point overhead to maximize
clock frequency.

Project Structure & File Purposes
---------------------------------

price_comparator.v: The core hardware design. 
Implements a 2-stage pipeline:
 - Stage 1: Registers incoming 32-bit price and threshold streams to isolate routing skew.
 - Stage 2: Performs a high-speed comparator check (price > threshold) and registers the final
boolean trigger flag.

tb_price_comparator.v: A self-checking testbench. Automatically drives test vectors, tracks 
pipeline delay using a behavioral reference model, and logs real-time PASS/FAIL diagnostics 
to the terminal.

waveform.vcd: Generated value change dump file containing simulation timing data for visual
inspection.

Getting Started & Prerequisites
------------------------------- 

To run this project locally using open-source EDA
tools, ensure you have Icarus Verilog (iverilog) and GTKWave installed on your Linux system.

How to Run the Simulation
-------------------------

Compile the design and testbench together:
- iverilog -o sim_run price_comparator.v tb_price_comparator.v

Execute the simulation:
- ./sim_run

View the timing waveforms (Optional):
- gtkwave waveform.vcd

